    "science": {
      "type": "kram-story-block",
      "settings": {
        "bundled_image": "kram-story-thread.jpg",
        "image_label": "Thread, spinning, or a new material under test — the craft meeting the laboratory.",
        "image_alt": "A maker winding spun cotton thread onto a skein winder",
        "ratio": "3 / 2",
        "image_position": "left",
        "eyebrow": "Craft and science",
        "heading": "Tradition, science, and design",
        "heading_size": "h2",
        "text": "<p>Sakuna’s approach combines traditional craftsmanship with modern science and design. KRAMSAKON has experimented with new textile treatments, contemporary products, and an indigo powder intended to make natural dyeing easier for a new generation of makers. The brand works alongside local producers on everything from clothing and scarves to bags and household textiles.</p>",
        "link_label": "",
        "link": "",
        "width": "page",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "padding_top": 88,
